{"id": 22, "ok": true, "cmd": "continuity", "ucas": "continuity floor(x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "continuity", "x": ["-9: jump from -10 to -9 (size 1) (f = -9 there)", "-8: jump from -9 to -8 (size 1) (f = -8 there)", "-7: jump from -8 to -7 (size 1) (f = -7 there)", "-6: jump from -7 to -6 (size 1) (f = -6 there)", "-5: jump from -6 to -5 (size 1) (f = -5 there)", "-4: jump from -5 to -4 (size 1) (f = -4 there)", "-3: jump from -4 to -3 (size 1) (f = -3 there)", "-2: jump from -3 to -2 (size 1) (f = -2 there)", "-1: jump from -2 to -1 (size 1) (f = -1 there)", "0: jump from -1 to 0 (size 1) (f = 0 there)", "1: jump from 0 to 1 (size 1) (f = 1 there)", "2: jump from 1 to 2 (size 1) (f = 2 there)", "3: jump from 2 to 3 (size 1) (f = 3 there)", "4: jump from 3 to 4 (size 1) (f = 4 there)", "5: jump from 4 to 5 (size 1) (f = 5 there)", "6: jump from 5 to 6 (size 1) (f = 6 there)", "7: jump from 6 to 7 (size 1) (f = 7 there)", "8: jump from 7 to 8 (size 1) (f = 8 there)", "9: jump from 8 to 9 (size 1) (f = 9 there)", "10: jump from 9 to 10 (size 1) (f = 10 there)"], "headline": "continuity of floor(x):"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "a grid of 20001 points, jumps located by bisection, limits from both sides; x has no range: searched [-10, 10]"}], "files": [], "text": "continuity of floor(x):\n  x = -9: jump from -10 to -9 (size 1) (f = -9 there)\n  x = -8: jump from -9 to -8 (size 1) (f = -8 there)\n  x = -7: jump from -8 to -7 (size 1) (f = -7 there)\n  x = -6: jump from -7 to -6 (size 1) (f = -6 there)\n  x = -5: jump from -6 to -5 (size 1) (f = -5 there)\n  x = -4: jump from -5 to -4 (size 1) (f = -4 there)\n  x = -3: jump from -4 to -3 (size 1) (f = -3 there)\n  x = -2: jump from -3 to -2 (size 1) (f = -2 there)\n  x = -1: jump from -2 to -1 (size 1) (f = -1 there)\n  x = 0: jump from -1 to 0 (size 1) (f = 0 there)\n  x = 1: jump from 0 to 1 (size 1) (f = 1 there)\n  x = 2: jump from 1 to 2 (size 1) (f = 2 there)\n  x = 3: jump from 2 to 3 (size 1) (f = 3 there)\n  x = 4: jump from 3 to 4 (size 1) (f = 4 there)\n  x = 5: jump from 4 to 5 (size 1) (f = 5 there)\n  x = 6: jump from 5 to 6 (size 1) (f = 6 there)\n  x = 7: jump from 6 to 7 (size 1) (f = 7 there)\n  x = 8: jump from 7 to 8 (size 1) (f = 8 there)\n  x = 9: jump from 8 to 9 (size 1) (f = 9 there)\n  x = 10: jump from 9 to 10 (size 1) (f = 10 there)\n  checked numerically: a grid of 20001 points, jumps located by bisection, limits from both sides; x has no range: searched [-10, 10]\n"}
{"id": 23, "ok": true, "cmd": "convexity", "ucas": "convexity x^3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "convexity", "inflection_points": "x = 0", "witness": "f(-1) = -1 > (f(-2) + f(0))/2 = -4", "proved_symbolically": "f'' = 6x, a polynomial; its sign changes only at real roots of odd multiplicity", "headline": "convexity of x^3:", "details": ["neither convex nor concave on all real x", "x in (-inf, 0]: concave (f'' < 0)", "x in [0, inf): convex (f'' > 0)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "convexity of x^3:\n  neither convex nor concave on all real x\n    x in (-inf, 0]: concave (f'' < 0)\n    x in [0, inf): convex (f'' > 0)\n  inflection points: x = 0\n  witness: f(-1) = -1 > (f(-2) + f(0))/2 = -4\n  proved symbolically: f'' = 6x, a polynomial; its sign changes only at real roots of odd multiplicity\n"}
{"id": 24, "ok": true, "cmd": "asymptotes", "ucas": "asymptotes (x^2+1)/x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "asymptotes", "vertical": "x = 0 (f -> -inf from the left, +inf from the right)", "oblique": "y = x as x -> ±inf", "proved_symbolically": "f = N/D with deg N = 2, deg D = 1; poles are the real roots of D that are roots of N of lower multiplicity (others are holes); at infinity the quotient of N by D", "headline": "asymptotes of (x^2 + 1)/x:"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "asymptotes of (x^2 + 1)/x:\n  vertical: x = 0 (f -> -inf from the left, +inf from the right)\n  oblique: y = x as x -> ±inf\n  proved symbolically: f = N/D with deg N = 2, deg D = 1; poles are the real roots of D that are roots of N of lower multiplicity (others are holes); at infinity the quotient of N by D\n"}
